      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by **never holding it there in the first place**. Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup\n2. **The key is injected only into the child process** \u2014 it\u0027s passed into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent immediately before that process starts\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment remains unmutated** \u2014 it never contains the credential\n\nThis design prevents a compromised or misbehaving Hub process from leaking the API key simply by inspecting environment variables, since the key only ever exists inside the short-lived child process that actually needs it (the one calling the Anthropic API). The Query agent process uses the same scoping model \u2014 it also receives the credential injected into its own environment at spawn time, never from the Hub.",
      "input_tokens": 5411,
